# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Yield token holders can drain value from principal token holders by manipulating ibt token exchange rate.

## Proof of Concept

Exchange rate of ERC-4626 [can be manipulated](https://www.euler.finance/blog/exchange-rate-manipulation-in-erc4626-vaults) and it can be done for profit by yt token holders.

On each yt token balance change ibtRate and ptRate are updated. ptRate can only [decrease](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-spectra/blob/383202d0b84985122fe1ba53cfbbb68f18ba3986/src/tokens/PrincipalToken.sol#L906-L912) and it happens in cases if currect exchange rate of ERC-4626 lower than stored rate, e.i. yield is negative. This condition can easily be triggered by anyone, naturally or on purpose. 

After that principal token amount [returned](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-spectra/blob/383202d0b84985122fe1ba53cfbbb68f18ba3986/src/tokens/PrincipalToken.sol#L667-L671) after maturity reduced permanently for principal token holders independent from future ibt rates.

PT token holders' ibt tokens doesn't disappear completely, they goes to yt token holders. So there is incentives for them to manipulate ibt exchange rate to theft principal from pt token holders.

