# Vulnerability details

## Impact
After expiry, users can manipulate rates to get more or less principal tokens for their underlying assets or vice versa when converting between the two. This could benefit certain users unfairly. 
It could enable certain attacks like flash loan arbitrage after expiry by artificially modifying rates. An attacker could take a flash loan, convert it to principal tokens using a manipulated low rate, redeem principal tokens using a manipulated high rate, and profit from it.
It goes against the concept of storing rates at expiry to finalize conversion rates. Allowing manipulation afterwards undermines this. Severity: Medium
