It was invoked on another function with the same name [PrincipalToken::withdrawIBT @ line 316](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-spectra/blob/383202d0b84985122fe1ba53cfbbb68f18ba3986/src/tokens/PrincipalToken.sol#L316) but this time, it has slippage protection as shown below.

```solidity
function withdrawIBT(
    uint256 ibts,
    address receiver,
    address owner,
    uint256 maxShares
) external override returns (uint256 shares) {
    shares = withdrawIBT(ibts, receiver, owner); // @audit invoked the function `withdrawIBT` line 303
