# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `PrincipalToken.sol` contract contains a function `claimRewards()` where `delegatecall()` is used. By creating a fake `IRewardsProxy` and providing properly-formatted calldata to the implementation contract, an attacker can gain control via the delegatecall() in order to selfdestruct() each implementation.

This is similar to the [Astaria beacon proxy issue](https://twitter.com/apoorvlathey/status/1671308196743647232?s=20)

## Proof of Concept
`PrincipalToken::claimRewards` (#L394-404)
```javascript
    function claimRewards(bytes memory _data) external restricted {
        if (rewardsProxy == address(0)) {
            revert NoRewardsProxySet();
        }
        _data = abi.encodeWithSelector(IRewardsProxy(rewardsProxy).claimRewards.selector, _data);
        (bool success, ) = rewardsProxy.delegatecall(_data);
        if (!success) {
            revert ClaimRewardsFailed();
        }
    }
```

